aging.py, doctor_locks.py x2); only staging.py compares the string for control flow","larval-tribal-tigermoth close-comment recorded the identical shared-symbol hazard: a second binding/contract change silently mis-serving a consumer"],"finding":"The plan changes the verdict strings returned by the shared `_describe_stamped_pid` (AC 5-7) but scopes edits to 'lock_owner.py plus regression tests', overlooking that `src/rebar/_store/staging.py._is_abandoned` is a behavioral consumer that branches on `verdict == 'live'` / `verdict == 'not-running'` (exact-string equality) to make a reclamation decision.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8450b252a7517521","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan ('Edit only src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py plus regression tests') + Acceptance Criteria lines 5-7","norm_id":"n9c5a9e95b5b85502","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["New unqualified-pid verdict returns a string other than 'live' (e.g. 'live (unverified)'): staging.py's `verdict == 'live'` no longer matches, so a genuinely-live staging owner is no longer protected by the early `return False` and reclamation defers to the age ceiling","A recycled/not-owner verdict string replaces 'not-running': staging.py's `verdict == 'not-running'` stops matching, delaying reclaim of an abandoned staging path"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Either keep `_describe_stamped_pid` returning the exact tokens `'live'`/`'not-running'` for the corroborated and dead cases (and add a distinct token only for the newly-refused unqualified case that staging.py already routes to the age ceiling), or explicitly widen scope to update staging.py's equality checks; correct the lock_owner.py:239 'DESCRIPTIVE ONLY' docstring accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_c