 plan changes the `_describe_stamped_pid` verdict-string contract (AC #5-7) and scopes edits to `lock_owner.py` + regression tests, but its affected-site inventory omits a real behavioral consumer of that string: `src/rebar/_store/staging.py:114` (`_is_abandoned`) branches on `verdict == \"live\"` / `verdict == \"not-running\"` to decide staging-dir reclamation. If an unqualified live pid stops rendering as `\"live\"`, that branch's outcome changes (staging falls through to the age ceiling), so this is not merely a diagnostic change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffa743224e4857e54","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan / AC #5–#7 (\"Edit only `src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py` plus regression tests\"; \"Holder diagnostics do not render an unqualified pid-number match as `pid_state=live`\")","norm_id":"na3dbd64a49247dd3","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["src/rebar/_store/staging.py `_is_abandoned`: on a same-host stamp whose pid is live but start-time unavailable (macOS, where `_process_start_time` returns None), a new verdict other than \"live\" flips the `verdict == \"live\"` branch — staging reclamation now depends on the age ceiling instead of holding, an unverified behavior change to a caller the plan does not name.","Any test covering staging-dir abandonment against a live-pid stamp would regress silently because the plan's Verification list names no staging test."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC and a pinned test for `_is_abandoned`'s behavior when `_describe_stamped_pid` returns the new unqualified-pid verdict, and either preserve the `\"live\"`/`\"not-running\"` string contract or update the `staging.py` equality checks accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satis